{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TiofdHScZRvNafHic1LbtH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0196R2dvHFqy9prYn8xxyFxS","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/log.md","old_string":"**Summary**: Split the per-AIR Round 0 loop into a sequential GPU phase (kernel launches + D2H copies) and a parallel CPU phase (transpose + iDFT via rayon). The improvement was only ~10ms (1.5%) at APC 300, well below the 10% rollback threshold. The 200ms gap between GPU kernel time and total Round 0 time is not dominated by CPU compute as hypothesized — it's primarily D2H copy latency and kernel launch overhead, which this optimization does not address.","new_string":"**Summary**: Split the per-AIR Round 0 loop into a sequential GPU phase (kernel launches + D2H copies) and a parallel CPU phase (transpose + iDFT via rayon). The improvement was only ~10ms (1.5%) at APC 300, well below the 10% rollback threshold. The 200ms gap between GPU kernel time and total Round 0 time is not dominated by CPU compute as hypothesized — it's primarily D2H copy latency and kernel launch overhead, which this optimization does not address.\n\n## 2026-04-12-2330-batch-stacked-reduction-mle-sync\n\n**Idea**: Eliminate per-window GPU synchronization in stacked reduction MLE rounds by batching all kernel launches with a single fill_zero + to_host per round.\n\n**Result**: success — Stacked Reduction at APC 300: 311ms → 126ms (2.47x lower vs baseline). STARK excl trace at APC 300: 2455ms → 2268ms (1.08x lower vs baseline). (vs previous: SR 312ms → 126ms, 2.48x lower; STARK 2460ms → 2268ms, -192ms)\n\n**Summary**: Replaced per-window D2H sync (to_host with pipeline drain) in batch_sumcheck_poly_eval with a single fill_zero + to_host per MLE round. Also bulk-uploaded eq_ub_per_trace once per round instead of per-window. At APC 300, MLE rounds dropped from 280ms to 95ms (2.95x), confirming that synchronization overhead was the dominant cost. APC 0 showed no regression."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":111,"cache_read_input_tokens":72137,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":111},"output_tokens":66,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"082795c8-8731-491f-857a-d4da84233f33","uuid":"f51ee175-2865-4d71-a308-5a06af93d221"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0196R2dvHFqy9prYn8xxyFxS","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/log.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"082795c8-8731-491f-857a-d4da84233f33","uuid":"234b7e94-4d7a-40ca-8f08-eddc79caa3f5","timestamp":"2026-04-12T22:09:13.354Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/log.md","oldString":"**Summary**: Split the per-AIR Round 0 loop into a sequential GPU phase (kernel launches + D2H copies) and a parallel CPU phase (transpose + iDFT via rayon). The improvement was only ~10ms (1.5%) at APC 300, well below the 10% rollback threshold. The 200ms gap between GPU kernel time and total Round 0 time is not dominated by CPU compute as hypothesized — it's primarily D2H copy latency and kernel launch overhead, which this optimization does not address.","newString":"**Summary**: Split the per-AIR Round 0 loop into a sequential GPU phase (kernel launches + D2H copies) and a parallel CPU phase (transpose + iDFT via rayon). The improvement was only ~10ms (1.5%) at APC 300, well below the 10% rollback threshold. The 200ms gap between GPU kernel time and total Round 0 time is not dominated by CPU compute as hypothesized — it's primarily D2H copy latency and kernel launch overhead, which this optimization does not address.\n\n## 2026-04-12-2330-batch-stacked-reduction-mle-sync\n\n**Idea**: Eliminate per-window GPU synchronization in stacked reduction MLE rounds by batching all kernel launches with a single fill_zero + to_host per round.\n\n**Result**: success — Stacked Reduction at APC 300: 311ms → 126ms (2.47x lower vs baseline). STARK excl trace at APC 300: 2455ms → 2268ms (1.08x lower vs baseline). (vs previous: SR 312ms → 126ms, 2.48x lower; STARK 2460ms → 2268ms, -192ms)\n\n**Summary**: Replaced per-window D2H sync (to_host with pipeline drain) in batch_sumcheck_poly_eval with a single fill_zero + to_host per MLE round. Also bulk-uploaded eq_ub_per_trace once per round instead of per-window. At APC 300, MLE rounds dropped from 280ms to 95ms (2.95x), confirming that synchronization overhead was the dominant cost. APC 0 showed no regression.","originalFile":"## 2026-04-12-2130-pipeline-round0-kernel-launches\n\n**Idea**: Eliminate per-AIR GPU synchronization in Round 0 by restructuring the loop into prepare/launch/collect phases.\n\n**Result**: failure — Round 0 at APC 300: 665ms → 645ms (1.03x lower vs baseline 662ms). STARK excl trace at APC 300: 2479ms → 2452ms (vs previous: -27ms, 1.01x lower).\n\n**Summary**: Restructured the Round 0 constraint evaluation from a per-AIR loop with 2 sync points each into three phases: prepare all metadata upfront, launch all kernels without sync, then batch-collect results. The improvement was only ~3% for Round 0 at APC 300 (20ms), well below the 10% rollback threshold. Root cause: the overhead is primarily CPU-side post-processing (transpose, iDFT) not GPU stall time, and cudaStreamPerThread already serializes kernels. Multi-stream parallelism or kernel fusion would be needed for meaningful gains.\n\n## 2026-04-12-2245-parallelize-round0-cpu-postprocess\n\n**Idea**: Parallelize CPU-bound post-processing (transpose, iDFT, polynomial construction) across AIRs using rayon in Round 0.\n\n**Result**: failure — Round 0 at APC 300: 667ms → 657ms (1.01x lower vs baseline 662ms). STARK excl trace at APC 300: 2468ms → 2455ms (vs previous: -13ms, 1.01x lower).\n\n**Summary**: Split the per-AIR Round 0 loop into a sequential GPU phase (kernel launches + D2H copies) and a parallel CPU phase (transpose + iDFT via rayon). The improvement was only ~10ms (1.5%) at APC 300, well below the 10% rollback threshold. The 200ms gap between GPU kernel time and total Round 0 time is not dominated by CPU compute as hypothesized — it's primarily D2H copy latency and kernel launch overhead, which this optimization does not address.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":3,"newStart":13,"newLines":11,"lines":[" **Result**: failure — Round 0 at APC 300: 667ms → 657ms (1.01x lower vs baseline 662ms). STARK excl trace at APC 300: 2468ms → 2455ms (vs previous: -13ms, 1.01x lower)."," "," **Summary**: Split the per-AIR Round 0 loop into a sequential GPU phase (kernel launches + D2H copies) and a parallel CPU phase (transpose + iDFT via rayon). The improvement was only ~10ms (1.5%) at APC 300, well below the 10% rollback threshold. The 200ms gap between GPU kernel time and total Round 0 time is not dominated by CPU compute as hypothesized — it's primarily D2H copy latency and kernel launch overhead, which this optimization does not address.","+","+## 2026-04-12-2330-batch-stacked-reduction-mle-sync","+","+**Idea**: Eliminate per-window GPU synchronization in stacked reduction MLE rounds by batching all kernel launches with a single fill_zero + to_host per round.","+","+**Result**: success — Stacked Reduction at APC 300: 311ms → 126ms (2.47x lower vs baseline). STARK excl trace at APC 300: 2455ms → 2268ms (1.08x lower vs baseline). (vs previous: SR 312ms → 126ms, 2.48x lower; STARK 2460ms → 2268ms, -192ms)","+","+**Summary**: Replaced per-window D2H sync (to_host with pipeline drain) in batch_sumcheck_poly_eval with a single fill_zero + to_host per MLE round. Also bulk-uploaded eq_ub_per_trace once per round instead of per-window. At APC 300, MLE rounds dropped from 280ms to 95ms (2.95x), confirming that synchronization overhead was the dominant cost. APC 0 showed no regression."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
